  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Required solver: OpenSees.\nBuild the spatial steel frame from the source coordinates, where source Y is up. Source X grid lines are 0, 6 and 10 m; source Z grid lines are 0 and 5 m; source Y levels are 0, 3 and 7 m (story heights 3 and 4 m). Use the exact right-handed orthogonal mapping (global X,Y,Z)=(source X,-source Z,source Y). Fix all six base nodes in all six degrees of freedom, transformed consistently with the coordinates. The only load is a nodal force at source (10,7,5) m with source components (20,-30,10) kN. It maps to global (10,-5,7) m and global force (20,-10,-30) kN in case D. Use the complete source/global node, restraint, member-axis and load tables in coordinate-transform.json. The appendix supplies Q355 steel (E=206000 MPa, nu=0.3, G=206000/2.6 MPa, density=7850 kg/m^3), solid rectangular columns C1=400x500 mm, source-X beams BX=300x600 mm and source-Z beams BY=250x500 mm. Section axes transform with the geometry; B and H remain attached to local y and z. Run OpenSees first-order linear elastic Euler-Bernoulli static analysis with self weight off. Report the loaded top corner displacement in both source and global three-component systems, all six global reaction components at every base, and all six local end-force components at both ends of c0-0-1, c2-1-1, c2-1-2, x0-0-2, x1-1-2 and y2-0-2. Supply transformed coordinate, load, restraint and local-axis tables with the result.\n\nUse all public appendices. Report the complete requested numerical table and the required summaries.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "input-data.json",
        "output-requests.json",
        "analysis-conventions.txt",
        "coordinate-transform.json"
      ],
      "unresolvedFields": [],
      "expectedQuestions": []
    }
  ],
